# Binaries a reader leaves behind running `go build ./quickstart`. The suite
# builds into a temporary directory and leaves nothing here.
#
# The negation is load-bearing: `/quickstart` matches the DIRECTORY of that name
# as well as the binary, and quickstart/ holds three tracked sample files. They
# stayed tracked because they were added before this rule, so nothing noticed —
# but every gitignore-respecting tool skipped them, and a fresh `git add -A`
# dropped them. A trailing slash restricts the negation to the directory, which
# leaves the binary ignored.
/quickstart
!/quickstart/
/out
